@@ -135,27 +142,49 @@ The sub-milestone that moved the loop procedures out of the policies and into wo
 
 Organize the stray audit and review-pass files in `workflow/coding-agent/` into proper workflows (operator, 2026-09-27). The core task is the coding-agent workflow consolidation: one canonical prompt per use case, the handover-audit pair merged, useful `kelsey-code-reviewer.skill.md` checks folded into `bash-audit.skill.md`, the non-current Claude-format imports (`dhh-code-audit.skill.md`, `architecture-doc-reviewer.skill.md`) dropped, `toc.sh` relocated out of skills, and the `audits/` folder dissolved while the `drafts/` folder gains a contract instead of dissolving -- the full disposition list is [`surface-area-report.md`](../.agents/audits/surface-area-report.md). For the documentation-audit use case, one pi-native prompt per [`documentation-audit-comparison.md`](../.agents/audits/documentation-audit-comparison.md), absorbing `architecture-doc-reviewer.skill.md` and `documentation-pass.md`.
 
-Also in scope, the review-pass family: the three framing fixes tracking the `2026-09-18` [AGENT_FEEDBACK](AGENT_FEEDBACK.md) entries -- round-cap and blocker re-review guidance for correctness reviews, naming the base commit and exact diff range in a review directive, and naming a seeded/runtime copy pair by full path with the authoritative copy stated; the review-pass workflow's required mutation step over the changed behaviour, the retirement of the reasoning-only assertion audit, and the adoption of the churn survey and fan-out protocol as standing passes with their triggers and frequency, with the bounded loop in [`review-loop-run.md`](../.agents/drafts/review-loop-run.md) as the first consumer of that review shape; and the exhaustive consistency pass -- a `-run`-family prompt that sweeps, once and exhaustively at the end of an iteration or a run, the classes that burn the late review rounds (documents that pin output strings, commands, exit semantics or count/shape contracts the change altered; one term spelled several ways across prompts, policies and records; counts repeated in records), with the judgement classes staying with the reviewer.
